Q: Header search paths with gcc using C_INCLUDE_PATH A: <p>in A.c:</p>

<pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
#include &lt;B.h&gt;

main()
{
    errPrint();
}
</code></pre>

<p>in B.c:</p>

<pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
#include &lt;B.h&gt;
void errPrint(void)   
{
    printf("err info\n");
}
</code></pre>

<p>If want to use <code>#include "file.h"</code> you gotta specified path example: <code>"/BBB/B.h"</code></p>

<p>For more info you can read  <a href="http://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n1124.pdf" rel="nofollow">In the C standard</a> section 6.10.2, paragraphs 2 to 4.</p>

<p><strong>EDIT</strong>: After test. try it please.</p>

<pre><code>echo -e "C_INCLUDE_PATH=/BBB\nexport C_INCLUDE_PATH" &gt;&gt; ~/.bash_profile

source ~/.bash_profile
</code></pre>

<p>and now</p>

<pre><code>gcc A.c B.c
</code></pre>

